      "widgets_values": [
        "Qwen3.5-2B",
        "cuda",
        "SDPA",
        "",
        "Refine",
        "Convert the user's Japanese scene description into ONE concise English prompt for the Anima anime image model.\nOutput a lowercase comma-separated tag line, followed only when useful by a blank line and 1-2 short English sentences.\nTags describe subject count, explicitly given characters, appearance, clothing, expression, pose, setting and lighting. Use spaces instead of underscores.\nSentences clarify only spatial relationships, interactions and framing that tags cannot express. Do not repeat appearance or clothing already stated in tags.\nPreserve the user's intent, subject count, attributes and camera instructions. If the request is brief, make it coherent without inventing character names, artists, major props or a different setting.\nDo not output quality or rating tags; the workflow adds them. Do not output headings, explanations, markdown fences, reasoning, alternatives, or Japanese.\nDo not add artist names or LoRA syntax. Preserve explicitly supplied English trigger words exactly. Avoid synonym duplication.",
        512,
        0.2,
        0.9,
        1.05,
        false,
        42,
        "fixed"
      ]
    },
